                                            "A kind of floodlight with a reflector."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "23fbea80-5cc2-31d4-8f5b-b74e55fa2fb8",
                                        "entry_id": "13c07711-edc3-374e-ad0b-9ca7254e6e92",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A haul of money made through speculation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "88834492-c9f5-3c28-a619-b3de5c024e01",
                                        "entry_id": "13c07711-edc3-374e-ad0b-9ca7254e6e92",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A note that begins slightly below and slides up to the target pitch."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9fb7ff4b-74f8-4b4e-9cab-729b0958bd82",
                                                "sense_id": "88834492-c9f5-3c28-a619-b3de5c024e01",
                                                "text": "Jazz symbols include many contoured articulations and inflections, such as doits, fall-offs, and scoops."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "scoop",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ebac434a-3828-3b70-84f3-a7f3b9ee466c",
                                        "entry_id": "3f04adac-c3af-3cb7-b18c-3d9aee5f110f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To lift, move, or collect with a scoop or as though with a scoop."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8012b20e-cbf3-4f15-87e3-75854683a9c6",
                                                "sense_id": "ebac434a-3828-3b70-84f3-a7f3b9ee466c",
                                                "text": "He used both hands to scoop water and splash it on his face."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6012d6c-81bb-447d-bac6-18b90ace4a0f",
                                                "sense_id": "ebac434a-3828-3b70-84f3-a7f3b9ee466c",
                                                "text": "Their first clear opportunity duly came courtesy of a mistake from Russell Martin, who was hustled off the ball by Bale, but the midfielder scooped his finish well over the top as he bore down on the Norwich goal."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "981cda2d-c7a0-3f86-9198-94f1318aca14",
                                        "entry_id": "3f04adac-c3af-3cb7-b18c-3d9aee5f110f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make hollow; to dig out."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa6c4288-ed6c-4950-a795-5e1b10622c80",
                                                "sense_id": "981cda2d-c7a0-3f86-9198-94f1318aca14",
                                                "text": "I tried scooping a hole in the sand with my fingers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "53e981fd-5528-310a-95fa-1de3697a4898",
                                        "entry_id": "3f04adac-c3af-3cb7-b18c-3d9aee5f110f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To report on something, especially something worthy of a news article, before (someone else)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "075c4abe-aea4-42e8-880e-c8428759b952",
                                                "sense_id": "53e981fd-5528-310a-95fa-1de3697a4898",
                                                "text": "The paper across town scooped them on the City Hall scandal."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4a6bf0a5-6e5a-3e3d-9337-2ced2db54ba4",
                                        "entry_id": "3f04adac-c3af-3cb7-b18c-3d9aee5f110f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To begin a vocal note slightly below the target pitch and then to slide up to the target pitch, especially in country music."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "often"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "93459aa6-b4ff-38c5-a810-ea9c6953cd98",
                                        "entry_id": "3f04adac-c3af-3cb7-b18c-3d9aee5f110f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To pick (someone) up"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "189ab6fa-ee54-4832-98a9-44d64342e6d0",
                                                "sense_id": "93459aa6-b4ff-38c5-a810-ea9c6953cd98",
                                                "text": "You have a car. Can you come and scoop me?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
